# Perl::Critic profile for this repo.
#
# Design: a curated, CORE-only profile gated at severity 4. It deliberately
# replaces an earlier 2287-line generated dump that ran at `severity = brutal`
# and referenced third-party policy bundles (OTRS, TryTiny, Bangs, logicLAB,
# Moose, Tics, StricterSubs, Reneeb's ProhibitAccessOfPrivateData, …) that are
# not part of the Perl::Critic distribution. Those bundles buried real findings
# in noise and only survived because `profile-strictness = warn` downgraded the
# resulting unknown-policy errors — "worse than nothing."
#
# This profile references ONLY policies shipped in the core Perl-Critic dist,
# so it is deterministic and matches the gate exactly: the pre-commit / CI gate
# runs perlcritic from a pinned `FROM perl + cpanm Perl::Critic` docker image
# (a controlled policy set with none of the machine's stray third-party
# bundles). NEVER reference a non-core policy here — the gate image would not
# have it installed, which would reintroduce the unknown-policy error the
# dropped `profile-strictness = warn` crutch used to mask.
#
# Severity ladder (see the dotagents repo's rules/perlcritic.md): 5 = most
# severe … 1 = brutal. We gate at 4 ("stern") and ratchet toward 1 in stages,
# cleaning each level's findings before tightening. Bump `severity` below to
# tighten; each step is tracked as a follow-up in TODO.md.

severity = 4
verbose  = %f:%l:%c [%p] %m (severity %s)\n
